PASS Every polished face is a mirror entry with its capture taken during preparation
PASS All mirror materials share one program key
PASS high: 2 mirrors reflect live, at most two drawn per frame
PASS balanced: 2 mirrors reflect live, at most two drawn per frame
PASS fast: 1 mirrors reflect live, at most two drawn per frame
PASS The best mirror draws at full size, the other at half
PASS A still camera redraws its live mirrors about every 100 ms, not every frame
PASS A moving camera redraws the best mirror every frame and the other in turn
PASS A live reflection restores the renderer state and the explorer
PASS A failed reflection restores the renderer state and stops reading its target
PASS The reflected camera clips at the mirror plane with an oblique near plane
PASS Leaving the live set blends back to the capture over about a quarter second
PASS A view through a door shows only the captures and keeps the live weights
PASS Leaving the court frees the live targets and keeps the captures
PASS Returning reflects live again
PASS Releasing the court's GPU resources frees every capture
PASS Restoring the court captures the mirrors again and reflects live
PASS No shader program was compiled by any of this
